(KEY-26 — `reap` is an expression: `reap any child process`,
 `reap process <pid>` and `reap child <pid>` all wait for a child and
 return its PID; reaping a PID that is not our child sets the error flag.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox KEY-26.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   reap any child returned the child pid
   reap child returned the child pid
   reap of a stranger set the error flag
)
Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Exit 0.
Set reaped to reap any child process.
If reaped is pid then,
    Print "reap any child returned the child pid".
Set another to fork the process.
If another is 0 then,
    Exit 0.
Set 'the second reaped' to reap child another.
If 'the second reaped' is another then,
    Print "reap child returned the child pid".
Set doomed to reap process 999999.
On error print "reap of a stranger set the error flag".
